---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import EditorialImage from '@components/EditorialImage.astro';
import ContactPanel from '@components/ContactPanel.astro';
import Card from '@components/Card.astro';
import image from '@assets/images/community-hands-together.webp';
---

<Layout
  title="Local social media support — Andrew Noblet"
  description="Thoughtful Facebook community-group posts for local businesses, with owner approval, group-rule review, and reply follow-up."
>
  <div class="editorial-page">
    <section class="editorial-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Social media support</p><h1>
          A local business.<br />A useful conversation.
        </h1><p>
          Help more neighbors understand what you do. I help write personal,
          useful Facebook community-group posts and follow up on the
          conversations they start.
        </p><div class="editorial-actions">
          <a class="editorial-button" href="/contact?service=social"
            >Discuss your business →</a
          ><a href="/services/social/pricing">Explore packages →</a>
        </div>
      </div><figure><EditorialImage src={image} priority /></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / From idea to follow-up</p><h2>
          Your knowledge.<br />Your voice.<br />Your approval.
        </h2><p>
          Start with a customer question, a service introduction, or a timely
          update. Each post uses details you confirm and gives readers a clear
          way to get in touch.
        </p>
      </div><ol class="process-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Understand</h3><p>
            Share your services, neighborhoods, photos, and the questions
            customers ask.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>Check the group</h3><p>
            Review group rules and posting permissions before planning the
            message.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>Review the draft</h3><p>
            You approve the wording. You or a person you choose publishes
            through your account.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>Follow the conversation</h3><p>
            Use the agreed reply support to handle questions and note useful
            inquiries.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Choose your rhythm</p><h2>
          Try one post.<br />Build from there.
        </h2><p>
          Use a one-time introduction to get started or choose a monthly package
          when you have regular updates to share.
        </p>
      </div><div class="editorial-grid">
        <Card
          ><h3>Community Post Starter</h3><p>
            One approved community post with group-rule review and 48 hours of
            reply monitoring. A $99 one-time package with no monthly commitment.
          </p><a href="/contact?package=Community%20Post%20Starter"
            >Discuss a first post →</a
          ></Card
        ><Card
          ><h3>Local Basic</h3><p>
            Four posts per month across one or two groups, reply handling, and a
            monthly one-page summary. $149 per month.
          </p><a href="/contact?package=Local%20Basic">Discuss Local Basic →</a
          ></Card
        ><Card
          ><h3>Local Pro</h3><p>
            Eight to twelve posts per month across two to four groups, message
            triage, basic metrics, and a monthly photo or video prompt. $299 per
            month.
          </p><a href="/contact?package=Local%20Pro">Discuss Local Pro →</a
          ></Card
        ><Card
          ><h3>Clear responsibilities</h3><p>
            Before starting, we confirm who approves, publishes, and answers
            customer questions. Results vary; we review visible responses and
            inquiries together.
          </p><a href="/services/social/pricing"
            >Compare packages and add-ons →</a
          ></Card
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Getting ready</p><h2>
          Bring what you<br />already know.
        </h2>
      </div><div class="editorial-prose">
        <p>
          You do not need a finished content plan. A short description of your
          business and the people you serve gives us a starting point.
        </p><ul>
          <li>
            Your services, service areas, and preferred contact method.
          </li><li>Questions customers commonly ask.</li><li>
            Photos you own or have permission to use.
          </li><li>Confirmed dates, offer terms, and availability.</li><li>
            The person who will approve, publish, and respond.
          </li>
        </ul><p>
          We can introduce your business, share practical advice, or explain an
          upcoming event. The aim is a helpful, honest post suited to the
          community, with one clear next step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactPanel
      title="What would you like your neighbors to know?"
      description="Bring a business page, a few notes, or an idea for a first post. We’ll talk through the support that fits your week."
      href="/contact?service=social"
    />
  </div>
</Layout>
